The [public Gitdex product page](https://aylith-labs.github.io/gitdex/) explains how to run Gitdex from source. It is a static landing page, **not a hosted inventory or a place to enter a GitHub token**.

## Actual frontend, fictional data

These light and dark captures come from Gitdex's unmodified Solid frontend running locally against a disposable loopback API. The two owners, four repositories, `.example.test` links, health scores, and staleness values are **synthetic fixtures**. No valid GitHub token was used, and the capture did not contact GitHub or exercise provider discovery and sync. The filter UI is real; the records in it are not.

